SPANISH 23

&


The following spanish mood rules are planned (* means:written):

\begin{description}
\item[Rmooddetermination*] finite declarative indicative   main clause
\item[Rmood2(indicativo)*]  finite declarative indicative   subordinate clause
\item[Rmood2(subjuntivo)*]  finite declarative subjunctive subordinate clause
\item[Rmood3*] finite wh-interrogative     indicative main clause
\item[Rmood4*] finite yes-no interrogative indicative main clause
\item[Rmood5*] finite yes-no interrogative indicative subordinate clause
\item[Rmood6*] finite wh-interrogative     indicative subordinate clause
\item[Rmoodfinrel*] finite relative        indicative subordinate clause
\item[Rmoodfinwhmod*] finite whmod         indicative subordinate clause
\item[Rmoodopeninf*] infinite declarative  infinitive subordinate clause, open
\item[Rmoodclosedinf*] infinite declarative  infinitive subordinate clause, closed
\item[Rmood7a*] finite imperative imperative main clause masculine singular
\item[Rmood7b*] finite imperative imperative main clause masculine plural
\item[Rmood8a*] finite imperative imperative main clause feminine singular
\item[Rmood8b*] finite imperative imperative main clause feminine plural
\item[Rmoodpoliteimp(masc/fem, sg/pl)*] finite imperative subjunctive main 
           clause polite masculine/feminine singular/plural
\item[Rmoodadhort1*] finite imperative subjunctive main clause 1pers. masc.
\item[Rmoodadhort2*] finite imperative subjunctive main clause 1pers. masc.
\item[Rmoodgerundio*] to form gerundial sentences
\item[RmoodPtcPas1*] to form participal clauses from ergative verbs
\item[RmoodPtcPas2*] to form participal clauses from passives 
\item[Rmood9] forming declarative subordinate future tense sentences.
generation only. For the mapping beloven te zwemmen - prometer que  nadar\'{a}

\end{description}

\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
%
% RULE RMooddetermination
                   (* Declarative main clause, finite, indicative *)
< m1:I2::CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
           [ I4:mu1,
             head/VERB{VERBrec1}
                        [I1:rel1/VERB{VERBrec2}[mu3],
                         mu4
                        ],
             mu5
           ] 
>

< m :I3::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}
             [ I4:mu1,
               head/VERB{VERBrec1}
                          [I1:rel1/VERB{VERBrec3}[mu3],
                           mu4
                          ],
               mu5
             ] 
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1 : rel1 IN [head,auxrel]
       I2 : CLAUSErec1.finiteness = finite  AND
            CLAUSErec1.tiempo <> omegatiempo AND
            CLAUSErec1.modo = omegamodo
       I3 : SENTENCErec1.tiempo <> omegatiempo AND
            SENTENCErec1 =
	           {
                    finiteness : finite
                    mood       : declarative
                    modo       : indicativo
                    senttype   : mainclause
                    conjkey    : 0
                    adverbial  : false
                    temporal   : false
                    conjclass  : omegaTimeAdvClass
                    conjtiempo : omegatiempo
                    conjaspecto: omegaAspecto
                    conjretro  : false
                   }
       I4: NOT EXIST(mu1, [I41:shiftrel/T1])
           I41: T1.CAT IN [NP, PREPP, ADVP, ADJP] WITH T1.REC.mood = wh
      >


      COMP
         <
          C1: VERBrec2.modo = omegamodo    AND
              CLAUSErec1.modo = omegamodo  AND
              (((VERBrec2.tiempo = pasado) AND
                (VERBrec2.futuro = nofuturo)
               ) -> 
               VERBrec2.aspecto <> omegaaspecto
              )
          A1: VERBrec3 := VERBrec2;
              VERBrec3.modo := indicativo;
              SENTENCErec1 := COPYT_clausetosentence(CLAUSErec1);
              SENTENCErec1 :=
		   {
                    mood     : declarative
                    senttype : mainclause
		   }
            (* other attributes retain default values *)
         >

      DECOMP
         <
          C1: VERBrec3.modo = indicativo AND
              (((VERBrec3.tiempo = pasado) AND
                (VERBrec3.futuro = nofuturo)
               ) ->
               VERBrec3.aspecto <> omegaaspecto
              )
          A1: VERBrec2 := VERBrec3;
              VERBrec2.modo := omegamodo;
              CLAUSErec1 := COPYT_sentencetoclause(sentencerec1);
              CLAUSErec1.modo := omegamodo
         >
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] RMooddetermination
\item[* relevant examples:]
CLAUSE[ (shiftrel/..) subjrel/\'{e}l compra libro] $\rightarrow$\\
SENTENCE [\'{e}l compra libro]
\item[* language:] Spanish
\item[* kind of rule:] M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] CLAUSEtoSENTENCE
\item[* class:] RCmooddetermination (?)
\item[* date of creation:] 9-MAY-1988 10:00:00  
\item[* author:] Elly van Munster
\item[* copied from:] Jan Odijk (RMooddetermination)
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 09/08/88\ \ \ \ \ author: Lisette Appelo
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To make a finite indicative main clause.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:]
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[\ \ consequences in the grammar:]
\item[\ \ translation aspects:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate} 
\item within this language:\\

\item in other languages:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[* relevant literature/documents:]
\item[\ \ remarks:]\mbox{}
\begin{itemize}
\item In Spanish, as opposed to Dutch, CLAUSE and SENTENCE do not have the 
attribute "modo" (Dutch "modus"), so only the {\em verb} is tested on (or 
assigned) "indicativo", not the CLAUSE/SENTENCE.
This is wrong, and has been adapted by JO {25/7/88}\\
In Spanish the indicativo can only be assigned to verbs with tiempo pasado if 
the aspecto is not omegaaspecto. LA (09/08/88)
\end{itemize}
\end{description}


% RULE Rmood2
                       (* finite, declarative, subordinate *)
< m1: I3::CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
                [ I5:sig3, 
                  I2:mu1,
                  head/VERB{VERBrec1}
                        [I1:rel1/VERB{VERBrec2}[mu3],
                         mu4
                        ],
                  mu2
                ]
>

< m : I4::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}
                           [I5:sig3, 
                            conjrel/CONJ(KEY_queconjkey){CONJrec1},
                            I2:mu1,
                            head/VERB{VERBrec1}
                                [ I1:rel1/VERB{VERBrec3}[mu3],
                                  mu4
                                ],
                            mu2
                           ]
>


   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1 : rel1 IN [head, auxrel]
       I5 : ALL(sig3, shiftrel/..) AND 
            NOT EXIST(sig3, [shiftrel/I51::NP{NPrec1}[mu7]])
            I51:NPrec1.mood = declxpmood
       I2 : NOT EXIST (mu1, [I12:rel2/..])
       I3 : CLAUSErec1.finiteness = finite
       I4 : SENTENCErec1.finiteness = finite
       I12: rel2 IN [leftdislocrel, shiftrel]
      >


   PARAMETERS
      <
       modopar  : modotype
      >




      COMP
         <
          C1: VERBrec2.modo = omegamodo AND
              CLAUSErec1.modo = omegamodo AND
              modopar IN [indicativo, subjuntivo] 
              C11: modopar = indicativo AND
                   (((VERBrec2.tiempo = pasado) AND
                     (VERBrec2.futuro = nofuturo)
                    ) -> 
                    VERBrec2.aspecto <> omegaaspecto
                   )
              A11: VERBrec3 := VERBrec2;
                   VERBrec3.modo := indicativo;
              C12: modopar = subjuntivo AND
                   (((VERBrec2.tiempo = pasado) AND
                     (VERBrec2.futuro = nofuturo)
                    ) ->
                    VERBrec2.aspecto = omegaaspecto
                   )
              A12: VERBrec3 := VERBrec2;
                   VERBrec3.modo := subjuntivo;
          A1: SENTENCErec1 := COPYT_clausetosentence(CLAUSErec1);
              SENTENCErec1 :=
		   {
 		    mood     : declarative
		    senttype : subordinateclause
                    modo     : modopar
                    conjkey  : KEY_queconjkey
		   }
            (* other attributes retain default values *)
         >

      DECOMP
         <
          C1: VERBrec3.modo IN [indicativo, subjuntivo] 
              C11: VERBrec3.modo =  indicativo AND
                   (((VERBrec3.tiempo = pasado) AND
                     (VERBrec3.futuro = nofuturo)
                    ) ->
                    VERBrec3.aspecto <> omegaaspecto
                   )
              A11: modopar := indicativo;
                   VERBrec2 := VERBrec3;
              C12: VERBrec3.modo = subjuntivo AND
                   (((VERBrec3.tiempo = pasado) AND
                     (VERBrec3.futuro = nofuturo)
                    ) ->
                    VERBrec3.aspecto = omegaaspecto
                   )
              A12: modopar := subjuntivo;
                   VERBrec2 := VERBrec3;
          A1: VERBrec2.modo := omegamodo;
              CLAUSErec1 := COPYT_sentencetoclause(sentencerec1);
              CLAUSErec1.modo := omegamodo;
         >

&

\end{verbatim}
